# Build output. Nothing generated belongs in the repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, this pattern matches any
# path component named "field-service" — including the cmd/field-service
# directory — so it did nothing here except hide main.go. That file assembles the
# whole service and was never committed, while git status reported a clean tree,
# because an ignored file is invisible to it.
/field-service
/dist/
